.SH NAME
xara\-monitor \- passive VARA HF traffic monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]xara\-monitor\f[R] (\f[B]\-\-wav\f[R] \f[I]FILE\f[R] |
\f[B]\-\-stdin\f[R] \f[I]RATE\f[R] | [\f[B]\-\-audio
pulse\f[R]|\f[B]alsa\f[R]] \f[B]\-\-capture\f[R] \f[I]SOURCE\f[R])
[\f[I]options\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]xara\-monitor\f[R] decodes VARA HF sessions between other stations
and prints timestamped details about the observed packets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-wav\f[R] \f[I]FILE\f[R]
PCM 8/16/24/32\-bit or float WAV at any rate
.TP
\f[B]\-\-stdin\f[R] \f[I]RATE\f[R]
s16le mono at \f[I]RATE\f[R] Hz (1000\-1000000) on stdin
.TP
\f[B]\-\-audio\f[R] pulse|alsa
Backend for \f[B]\-\-capture\f[R] (default pulse, alsa when pulse is not
present)
.TP
\f[B]\-\-capture\f[R] \f[I]SOURCE\f[R]
Pulse source or ALSA PCM, opened capture\-only.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-hf\f[R] 500|2300|2750
HF bandwidth (default: 2300)
.TP
\f[B]\-\-call\f[R] \f[I]CALL\f[R]
Known call sign (repeatable)
.TP
\f[B]\-\-calls\f[R] \f[I]FILE\f[R]
List of known calls, one per line.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-no\-blind\f[R]
Only attempt to resolve known calls
.TP
\f[B]\-\-key\-idle\f[R] \f[I]MIN\f[R]
Max target idle time (default: 30, 0 disables)
.TP
\f[B]\-\-log\f[R] \f[I]FILE\f[R]
Append UTC\-timestamped output to \f[I]FILE\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-\-dump\f[R]
Dump entire payloads
.TP
\f[B]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Report unconfirmed blind detections
.TP
\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]
Print newline\-delimited JSON records.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ui\-port\f[R] \f[I]N\f[R]
Serve the web UI (read\-only) on port \f[I]N\f[R], with bonus content at
\f[B]/stream\f[R].
Disabled by default.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ui\-addr\f[R] \f[I]ADDR\f[R]
Listen address for the web UI (default 127.0.0.1).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ui\-host\f[R] \f[I]NAME\f[R]
Also accept \f[I]NAME\f[R] as HTTP Host for UI (repeatable)
.TP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\-\-help\f[R], \f[B]\-V\f[R], \f[B]\-\-version\f[R]
Print the usage or the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 at the end of the input, on the first SIGINT or SIGTERM, or when
standard output is closed; 1 on an error; 2 on a bad command line; 130
on a second signal.
